github_url: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-hypothesis/issues/5"
body: "## Summary\n\nThe public SDK changes valid exact observation keys and values before returning them. Following `nextRequest` and feeding its returned key/value into `observe` can leave hypotheses unresolved or eliminate the very hypothesis whose predicted value was selected.\n\nReproduced on PR #1 at `a7ff9519c4b7155859d331a9f79fd6b41749dafb`, package version `2026.10.25`, Node `24.22.1`, and the pinned `@unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.24`. Only a fresh synthetic filesystem tracker was used.\n\n## Minimal SDK reproduction\n\nSave as `repro.ts` at that checkout's root and run `node repro.ts` with its dependencies available:\n\n```ts\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { mkdtemp, rm } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\nimport { PmClient } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk';\nimport { open, add, nextRequest, observe, matrix } from './index.ts';\n\nconst root = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'hypothesis-roundtrip-'));\ntry {\n  const workspace = join(root, '.agents', 'pm');\n  const client = new PmClient({ pmRoot: workspace, author: 'fixture', noExtensions: true });\n  await client.init('hyp', { defaults: true, agentGuidance: 'skip', mergeFence: false });\n  const options = { workspace, author: 'fixture' };\n  const { investigation } = await open('Synthetic latency incident', options);\n  const a = await add(investigation, 'Below threshold',\n    [{ observation: 'latency', value: '<500ms' }], options);\n  await add(investigation, 'Above threshold',\n    [{ observation: 'latency', value: '>500ms' }], options);\n  const request = (await nextRequest(investigation, options)).request!;\n  const selected = request.groups.find(g => g.hypotheses.includes(a.hypothesis))!;\n  await observe(investigation, request.observation, selected.value, options);\n  const result = await matrix(investigation, options);\n  console.log({ selected: selected.value, statuses: result.rows.map(r => r.status) });\n  assert.equal(result.rows.find(r => r.id === a.hypothesis)!.status, 'viable');\n} finally {\n  await rm(root, { recursive: true, force: true });\n}\n```\n\nExpected: the selected value is the original `<500ms`; the matching hypothesis is viable and the alternative is eliminated.\n\nActual: the selected value contains a literal backslash-u escape, `\\\\u003c500ms`. Both hypotheses are eliminated because that value equals neither original prediction.\n\nAn independent key-only case also fails: predictions on `latency<500ms` return the key `latency\\\\u003c500ms`. Observing that returned key leaves both hypotheses unknown, since the new fact targets a different key.\n\n## Cause and impact\n\n[`nextRequest`](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-hypothesis/blob/a7ff9519c4b7155859d331a9f79fd6b41749dafb/src/hypothesis.ts#L76-L80) calls `safe` before returning structured data. [`safe` and `inert`](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-hypothesis/blob/a7ff9519c4b7155859d331a9f79fd6b41749dafb/src/core.ts#L19-L21) replace characters inside strings rather than applying an output serialization escape. [`matrix` and `resumePacket`](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-hypothesis/blob/a7ff9519c4b7155859d331a9f79fd6b41749dafb/src/hypothesis.ts#L71-L92) use the same transformation.\n\nThe transformation is also non-injective: a real `<` and the literal six-character string `\\\\u003c` produce the same returned text. A caller cannot reliably repair this by decoding escapes. This affects machine consumers and copied CLI values, not the underlying equality comparison, which correctly compares the changed observation against the original data.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Returned observation keys and predicted values can be passed unchanged from `nextRequest` into `observe`.\n- Matrix/resume machine-readable fields preserve exact values or expose an unambiguous lossless representation.\n- Distinguish real controls/markup from literal backslash-u sequences.\n- Keep terminal rendering inert at the presentation boundary rather than changing SDK data semantics.\n- Add round-trip regression coverage for keys and values containing `<`, `>`, backticks, newline/control characters, and literal escape strings.\n\nCanonical owner: [pm-hypothesis PR #1](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-hypothesis/pull/1). The fault occurs in this package before the host SDK receives the observation. This is a focused correctness reproduction, not a full release or remote-backend certification.\n\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-25T15:32:36Z)\n>\n> Verified source follow-through at PR #1 head `14b01509251de3e617bfabaee61d81d57747ef45` (Node 24.22.1, exact cached SDK 2026.10.24, TypeScript 7.0.2, TOON 4.4.0): the original reproduction in this issue now passes. `nextRequest` returns the original `<500ms`, and passing it unchanged to `observe` leaves the selected hypothesis viable and the alternative eliminated.\n> \n> The revision moves escaping to the transport boundary and preserves reusable SDK keys/values. Independent isolated checks also pass:\n> - Source typecheck and build.\n> - 9/9 sequential workflow/restoration/round-trip tests, including 64 seeded key cases across TOON and JSON plus native CLI control-byte transport.\n> - 4/4 native-command/property tests, including 100 seeded derivation sets.\n> \n> These are tests of the pinned PR source in disposable synthetic trackers, not evidence of a merge or npm publication. No dependencies or original checkout were changed. Full release/coverage and concurrent-writer certification are not claimed; issue #6 is a separate remaining initialization-retry problem."
